{
 "about": "Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1+2 (CC0) retargeted onto Godot-chan by blender/tools/retarget_ual.py. 'clips' adds each source clip under a scheme name (character_anim_naming.json); 'replace' writes a source clip (or 'A+B', played one after the other) INTO an existing placeholder action, keeping its name, so the AnimationTree picks it up with no scene edit. A_TPose is skipped: the rig's own tpose is the reference. A replace value may be {src, arms_over}: only the arms (clavicles down) take the source, in WORLD directions, over the named action's first-frame pose -- for clips the tree plays through an arms filter. 'Clip@N' holds one frame as a static loop. 'Clip@A:B' takes frames A..B. A 'clips' value may also be {name, arms_over}. 'drop' removes a clip (death_fall_back: the ragdoll is the death, CLAUDE.md W35). 'fist_axis' [x,y,z] (armature space) turns only the right wrist so a held handle points that way: melee and throwable hold the FIST's guard with the weapon stood up, 20 deg forward (W36).",
